Ticket #4471 merged 412 reports of dates landing on the wrong day. Analysis identified two distinct problems, both of which the desk has now resolved.

<Callout>
Closed 5 October. Parser fixed. Hint form retired.
</Callout>

## The two problems

### 1. Parser reads MM/DD for all locales — 414 reports

The date parser unconditionally interpreted dates as MM/DD without respecting locale.

**Resolution:** Fixed in commit `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.

**GitHub Issue:** [#71](https://github.com/piotrczarnak/mega/issues/71)

### 2. Form hint displays MM/DD for day-first tenants — 13 reports

Booking-v3 form displayed MM/DD/YYYY hint, confusing users in day-first locales.

**Resolution:** Won't fix. Booking-v3 form has been retired.

**GitHub Issue:** [#72](https://github.com/piotrczarnak/mega/issues/72)

## Lessons

- Merge early, count once. One big ticket held two separate bugs.
- Write the page while the resolution is fresh.
